# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

~> **Safety** Switching the VLAN mode discards the VLAN settings of the other modes (the vendor utility warns about this) and can cut every connection, including the management path. The provider refuses to change the mode unless `allow_disruptive = true`; applying the mode the switch already has writes nothing. Do it on a switch you can reach another way, with a fresh configuration backup (`tplinkeasysmart_config_backup`). On the verified firmware (20250710), enabling `802.1q` created VLAN 1 with every port untagged and PVID 1, so the management path through the uplink stayed up; going back to `port-based` restored the port-based VLAN 1 with all ports. The MTU VLAN was not exercised live: with it on, only the uplink port can talk to the others, so a wrong `mtu_uplink_port` cuts the management path.

